<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>South Africans vote in key municipal elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25a66d58c2733e096233d02f0821e12688ea19de1a96352c4059e78ab6812a25</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:26:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africans-vote-in-key-municipal-elections" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, a crucial test for South Africa's  ruling ANC as millions vote to elect municipal governments. Also, Ethiopia has expelled six Sudanese diplomats amid accusations it's allowing the paramilitary RSF to launch drone strikes from its territory. And a deepening humanitarian crisis in Ethiopia, where renewed fighting has displaced thousands.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo residents sue Chinese mining giant for widespread pollution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc036dd1834ee8d4047e6b2ecaf0d1307dd0e389edf5e378ffa47243dcbd520f</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:22:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-dr-congo-residents-sue-chinese-mining-giant-for-widespread-pollution" /><summary type="html">In Kolwezi, the mining capital of the Democratic Republic of Congo, local residents are suing a huge Chinese mine and the government for environmental pollution. It will be one of the most important cases the country has seen. FRANCE 24's correspondent Emmet Livingstone reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>30 million South Africans registered to vote across nine provinces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:179e7a83a3279456463cb83a08ee1f3c622ea16ee505292ac71d693c5ae68684</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:20:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-30-million-south-africans-registered-to-vote-across-nine-provinces" /><summary type="html">In South Africa, around 30 million people have registered to cast their votes across the country's nine provinces. The economy is at the forefront of the November 4 local elections. The spotlight is on Gauteng, a province long plagued by governance challenges. FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Sudanese Arab refugees face hostility and distrust after fleeing to Chad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c2d9edff73c675e5e7d5c151e1c3246288e53d90db245ba3061dafad9d71f94</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:18:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-sudanese-arab-refugees-face-hostility-and-distrust-after-fleeing-to-chad" /><summary type="html">Thousands of Arab Sudanese who have arrived in Chad after fleeing fighting at home are facing mistrust and hostility from fellow Sudanese refugees. Fighters linked to the Rapid Support Forces, whose ranks are largely drawn from Sudan’s Arab communities, have been accused of repeatedly targeting civilians from other ethnic groups. FRANCE 24's Harold Girard reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Washington excludes South Africa and Rwanda from US duty-free trade deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67a1e8ca3fb717c8268d26f75275e1ed81414f67bff75308758f0a21efbb59b9</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:15:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261104-washington-excludes-south-africa-and-rwanda-from-us-duty-free-trade-deal" /><summary type="html">South African and Rwandan exporters are weighing potential job losses and squeezed margins after Washington decided to exclude them from the AGOA program, the African Growth and Opportunity Act, ending the countries' duty-free access to the US market. Economists warned against "alarmist" reactions to the exclusion and argue the broader economic fallout will likely be limited.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa braces for some job losses as AGOA ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a71e655de48f8f08eeadd9e1239c21a958cce0da323cbb7ce903fb562f4a8be</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T21:18:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-braces-for-some-job-losses-as-agoa-ends" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Rwanda and South Africa will lose their duty-free access to the US market after being excluded from the AGOA trade programme. Also, South Africans head to the polls amid water shortages and frustration with local services. Plus in DR Congo's mining capital Kolwezi, residents are taking on one of the country's largest Chinese-owned mines, accusing it of poisoning their environment.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal's opposition-dominated parliament rejects revised budget bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9253760d790d29982425fb6ffc2630ece3474634490393dea6b2901aff6db4a1</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:40:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261103-senegal-powerful-opposition-rejects-crucial-budget-bill--942d392c755d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261103-senegal-powerful-opposition-rejects-crucial-budget-bill" /><summary type="html">Senegal's powerful opposition party Pastef led by former presidential candidate Ousmane Sonko on Tuesday rejected a revised version of the country's budget, leaving the west African nation's new bailout programme with the International Monetary Fund hanging in the balance.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda withdraws its troops from Somalia as fight against rebels persists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d77cf4c7f067ed7474cfae12253b808edf2935f043b0fb31023070f992aaf487</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:50:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-uganda-withdraws-its-troops-from-somalia-as-fight-against-rebels-persists--878da3c15104.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-uganda-withdraws-its-troops-from-somalia-as-fight-against-rebels-persists" /><summary type="html">Kampala announced on Monday it had begun pulling its troops out of Somalia. Uganda was the first country to send deployments to help Mogadishu when the African Union set up an international military mission in 2007 to battle al-Shabab extremist rebels. But what is prompting Kampala to withdraw its troops now, as the battle against the militants continues? FRANCE 24’s Georga Calvin Smith is joined by Horn of Africa geopolitical analyst Anwar Abdifatah Bashir.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africans demand security and basic services as they vote in local elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c12f86d334f756ae3c5ed7a761e71ecaf42351061f40f0be454a6ae7c02ff4af</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:39:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-south-africans-demand-security-and-basic-services-as-they-vote-in-local-elections--7b95b95f6073.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-south-africans-demand-security-and-basic-services-as-they-vote-in-local-elections" /><summary type="html">High crime rates and a lack of basic services are causing concern among many of South Africa’s 29 million registered voters. Water shortages and unreliable electricity supplies have also become symbols of municipal failures, angering voters and eroding support for the ruling African National Congress. The municipal elections on November 4 will offer a glimpse into whether these frustrations are shifting political loyalties.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo opposition figure Prince Epenge arrested for spreading fake news</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e36483c39095e5830baa13a1cd31b58a2efc50b9a7d272b5c1650e1c9a89baa</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:27:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-dr-congo-opposition-figure-prince-epenge-arrested-for-spreading-fake-news--7f5a93d10bc1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-dr-congo-opposition-figure-prince-epenge-arrested-for-spreading-fake-news" /><summary type="html">DR Congo senior opposition leader Prince Epenge has been arrested and transferred to prison. He is being held on charges of spreading fake news. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kinshasa, Emmet Livingstone, has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Chadian farmers suffer from intensifying drought and take stock of their losses</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d3b06638f32871d181cd808191d931384714d5f301c67a42e1c48e6fe5eae7e</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:26:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-chadian-farmers-suffer-from-intensifying-drought-and-take-stock-of-their-losses--5569a10d9ea7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-chadian-farmers-suffer-from-intensifying-drought-and-take-stock-of-their-losses" /><summary type="html">In Chad, Wadi Fira is one of the two regions hardest hit by the drought. Just a few kilometres outside Biltine, the regional capital, farmers take stock of their devastating losses. FRANCE 24's Harold Girard reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Uganda withdraws troops from peacekeeping mission in Somalia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c4bf6e909792e616fde3f327d25b90ea51bcd7de6879b6a2dbe841fdb9a986e</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T21:24:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uganda-withdrawing-troops-from-peacekeeping-mission-in-somalia--de085b5a97a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uganda-withdrawing-troops-from-peacekeeping-mission-in-somalia" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Uganda starts drawing down troops just days after the UN ends its political mission in Somalia. Also, upcoming municipal elections in South Africa risk solidifying growing political fragmentation. Plus the drought gripping Chad could be the country's worst in more than 40 years.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>UN’s peacekeeping mission in disputed Western Sahara ends after 35 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a0b2eee4eb1dd6bdfb5deefdf5f30d9d4ab51f9980dd1c1d91fdda9e879aaab</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T20:37:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261101-un-s-peacekeeping-mission-in-disputed-western-sahara-ends-after-35-years--307cf640fd2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261101-un-s-peacekeeping-mission-in-disputed-western-sahara-ends-after-35-years" /><summary type="html">The 35-year-old UN peacekeeping mission ⁠in the disputed Western ​Sahara region came to an end Sunday after the Security Council failed to ​renew its mandate. Morocco, which claims the region as its own, welcomed the decision, while its opponents from the Algeria-backed Polisario Front called it "unacceptable".</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal hosts first Olympic event on African continent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a595e9201995a15e53f40eaf455efa47ace6e06ea6fe41b827aef74fa5557fa</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:58:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/senegal-hosts-first-olympic-event-on-african-continent--b512a9a9b84e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/senegal-hosts-first-olympic-event-on-african-continent" /><summary type="html">Youth Olympics make history with first African Games in over 130 years, opened by Senegal’s president in Dakar. 136 Senegalese athletes are competing, supported by 6,000 local volunteers.</summary></entry><entry><title>Youth Olympic Games kick off in Dakar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ecf8eec608e8d5003edafb0ae9042975f7c1f224b612162d7618fef1e73c848f</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T09:49:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/youth-olympic-games-kick-off-in-dakar--423e308b5a0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/youth-olympic-games-kick-off-in-dakar" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Youth Olympic Games have officially kicked off in Senegal. Crowds gathered for Saturday's opening ceremony, featuring hundreds of drummers and dancers celebrating Senegalese and wider African culture, in keeping with the Games' motto: “Africa welcomes, Dakar celebrates”. It is the first-ever Olympic sporting event to be held on the African continent, but comes as Senegal faces an economic crisis. The country's president has said he wants to turn sport into an “economic and social engine”. The Games also come amid a government crackdown on LGBTQ+ people. Nearly 3,000 teenagers from more than 200 countries are competing in around a dozen sports, including athletics, beach wrestling and a five-a-side version of baseball. Jean-Loup Chappelet, Professor at Lausanne University and Olympics specialist, shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Senegal kicks off Africa's first ever Olympics with Youth Games</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5879cd826cba666675b5e1680929548744542d968f381c7f1edae7f90582c569</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T09:37:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261031-senegal-hosts-africa-s-first-ever-youth-olympic-games--48359a071e4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261031-senegal-hosts-africa-s-first-ever-youth-olympic-games" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Youth Olympic Games opened on Saturday in the Senegalese capital Dakar in the first-ever Olympics to be held on African soil. It comes as the continent seeks a bigger role in international sporting competitions.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>First Youth Olympic Games take place in Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41393fe596ee25aace5bab6754f9c0ec1fc2fec32402bb11f906a6b0298011ef</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T21:48:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/first-youth-olympic-games-in-africa--c6de06960cd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/first-youth-olympic-games-in-africa" /><summary type="html">In tonight's show: The Senegalese capital Dakar is hosting the first Olympic event ever held in Africa, welcoming nearly 2,700 athletes for the 2026 Youth Olympic Games. Also, South Africa's local elections are set for November 4, with the African National Congress facing growing pressure over its record in local government. Finally, we're joined by Muse L'Artiste, who's reconnecting to her roots with her latest EP "Heritage" bringing her father's compositions back to life.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Russia recruits Africans to fight in Ukraine, families seek answers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19fc32209d64a53ab9ccde735084336d85bd226e95c7d213d0150952c0ed435e</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:06:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-recruits-africans-to-fight-in-ukraine-families-seek-answers--daeb7f5e2250.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-recruits-africans-to-fight-in-ukraine-families-seek-answers" /><summary type="html">While African leaders and Russian officials gather to discuss security, trade and political cooperation at the Africa-Russia summit, one sensitive issue is notably absent from the agenda: the recruitment of Africans to fight for Russia in Ukraine. More than 1,400 Africans have been enlisted since 2023. In Tunisia, concern is growing as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for answers about the fate of their loved ones. FRANCE 24's team in Tunisia reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least 60 Christians killed in Ethiopia amid rising religious violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb2dba5b948f04b471a8205397cb8d8fe430b6589ef3253c20bbcc55ad783a0c</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:01:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-at-least-60-christians-killed-in-ethiopia-amid-rising-religious-violence--6a05b4f64af9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-at-least-60-christians-killed-in-ethiopia-amid-rising-religious-violence" /><summary type="html">At least 60 Christians have been killed in Ethiopia in what the Orthodox Church has declared as religious violence. It is still unclear who was behind the attack, with rebels and local government blaming each other. Around 20 houses have been burned down, as FRANCE 24's correspondent Tom Canetti reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Senegal gears up for historic 2026 Youth Olympic Games in Dakar</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6813c00981d83ba48790edc376e9a8f9b9575d9f7d3c9f727c1ca298685ff74</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-senegal-gears-up-for-historic-2026-youth-olympic-games-in-dakar--bbbedcbc2dcf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-senegal-gears-up-for-historic-2026-youth-olympic-games-in-dakar" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee is upbeat just 24 hours before competition gets under way at the 2026 Youth Olympic Games in Senegal. Venues are ready to host the first-ever Olympic event on the African continent. FRANCE 24's correspondent Aminatou Diallo reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tanzania: 2025 election violence still traumatises, one year on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db5f86435896fa5b9c223336385bdcc45c9b80ae15b708e09a8b5112e3efbd3f</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T10:55:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-tanzania-2025-election-violence-still-traumatises-one-year-on--b9669e9b3291.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261030-tanzania-2025-election-violence-still-traumatises-one-year-on" /><summary type="html">Tanzania is marking the first anniversary of a bloody election that left many traumatised. The October 29, 2025 election, in which President Samia Suluhu Hassan won with 98 percent of the vote after most of the opposition was excluded, triggered days of protests that security forces brutally suppressed. Many government critics say they still fear abduction, arbitrary arrest and politically motivated prosecutions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tunisians drawn into Russia's war in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d24e4299c79c5850fecd2b3284e132c28548e72c2410348a169c77c6a7bb34d6</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T21:48:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tunisians-drawn-into-russia-s-war-in-ukraine--3c814c58dec2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tunisians-drawn-into-russia-s-war-in-ukraine" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Concern is growing in Tunisia as the families of several men who travelled to Russia for work or study are still searching for an answer about the fate of their loved ones forcibly conscripted to the war in Ukraine. Also, a year after Tanzania's controversial election, fear hasn't faded. And Dakar is ready to make history, as the first Olympic event ever held on African soil gets underway this weekend.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Across Africa: Real estate scams on the rise in Ivory Coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7680fa90b9e78db68b3a9b3a36bde2b164763799ec6bc5ee27d3df6475ea5d10</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T21:43:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/across-africa-real-estate-scams-growing-in-ivory-coast--1b8d25568bef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/across-africa-real-estate-scams-growing-in-ivory-coast" /><summary type="html">This week in Across Africa: In Ivory Coast, a severe housing shortage has fuelled demand for land, creating opportunities for fraudsters selling fake properties and non-existent plots. Also, Kenya's women are changing the game. From the track to the boxing ring, female athletes are delivering some of the country’s biggest sporting successes. Plus Addis Ababa pushes ahead with ambitious plans to become East Africa's clean-energy powerhouse.</summary><category term="Across Africa" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo: A centre celebrates the discharge of last Ebola patients</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d078bbcbd5e2e83fcc7d5b1625a9852c866716bf92efc1204eab734bbf334a94</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T17:13:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-dr-congo-a-centre-celebrates-the-discharge-of-last-ebola-patients--1a7209d31c3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-dr-congo-a-centre-celebrates-the-discharge-of-last-ebola-patients" /><summary type="html">Medical staff and residents at a treatment centre in Ituri danced and sang to celebrate a first since May: the centre is no longer treating any confirmed Ebola cases.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin seeks to expand ties with African countries at Russia-Africa summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d04c1510388cd32d07e484f16d3a5da3b80880aa2a918dcd24e2edc51fd8dac</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:32:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-putin-seeks-to-expand-ties-with-african-countries-at-russia-africa-summit--7fe29c8b00d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-putin-seeks-to-expand-ties-with-african-countries-at-russia-africa-summit" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin on Wednesday hosted dozens of African leaders at a Russia-Africa summit, part of Moscow’s efforts to expand its influence across the continent. The Russia-Africa summit marks a renewed Kremlin effort to bolster ties with a continent of nearly 1.6 billion people that is increasingly assertive on the global stage.</summary></entry><entry><title>DRC: C64 opposition coalition meets in Rome, calls for inclusive dialogue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e277937842e9a381a2f04c7501ca3e2a478bdb31297f7888555afc2028a0d7af</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:28:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-drc-c64-opposition-coalition-meets-in-rome-calls-for-inclusive-dialogue--2673a39bc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-drc-c64-opposition-coalition-meets-in-rome-calls-for-inclusive-dialogue" /><summary type="html">Democratic Republic ⁠of Congo's main ​opposition coalition, C64, met in Rome on Tuesday. Under pressure to respond to Joseph Kabila’s rebellion, its five leaders addressed the situation in the country from the Italian capital. They condemned any seizure of power by force and called for inclusive dialogue. FRANCE 24’s Emmet Livingston reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Niger: Guards accused of 'cruel, inhuman' treatment after 33 die in detention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf0aaa83648e0821ea4caf46258415b2ab80ba396095ec25b7a276566dcb6c62</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:17:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-niger-guards-accused-of-cruel-inhuman-treatment-after-33-die-in-detention--06ca18f6c774.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-niger-guards-accused-of-cruel-inhuman-treatment-after-33-die-in-detention" /><summary type="html">In Niger, guards ignored the panicked cries for help from 33 detainees who died in a detention cell last month. Reports indicate that 72 people were crowded into a poorly ventilated, 20-square-metre space, where dozens slowly suffocated over 11 hours. The cell may have been cleaned and disinfected before it could be investigated. FRANCE 24's correspondent Sam Olukoya has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenya's female athletes make their mark as Youth Olympic Games approach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57901ff1cb371656501cd0b0dfb2ebea4f7fe7eda09e0afa0c148f75c11e2966</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:45:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-kenya-s-female-athletes-make-their-mark-as-youth-olympic-games-approach--fa8c0d0a87ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-kenya-s-female-athletes-make-their-mark-as-youth-olympic-games-approach" /><summary type="html">Senegal is preparing to host the Youth Olympic Games, which begin this weekend. The young athletes who hope to showcase their talents on the international stage have their sights set on the Games, and Kenya has made sure that its young boxers remain on their toes and are ready to take on opponents of a higher calibre. FRANCE 24's Bastien Renouil reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Somalia: Lower house of parliament passes bill on sexual violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a233dcb78c89e52cd24f97f0d90fcf4b5a59e506a1a2144b98fa1f2d85e20d5</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:42:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-somalia-lower-house-of-parliament-passes-bill-on-sexual-violence--471d5dd22da0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261029-somalia-lower-house-of-parliament-passes-bill-on-sexual-violence" /><summary type="html">The Somali Parliament has passed a new law against sexual violence. The country’s criminal code dated back to 1962 and had not been updated since. FRANCE 24's Bastien Renouil met with Sofia Rajab in Nairobi. She is the program manager at the NGO Legal Action Worldwide, an organisation that lobbied Somali authorities in support of this new law.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia woos African leaders at Moscow summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1669d833f54946638bf3ac1839424fdf248cb374a12bd92cb7ee0992a287fcd5</id><updated>2026-11-04T21:59:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T21:27:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-woos-african-leaders-at-moscow-summit--0fad5419a542.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-woos-african-leaders-at-moscow-summit" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: A summit with nearly two dozen African leaders opens in Moscow, with the Kremlin describing their countries as natural allies against the West. Also, Nigerian investigators say that dozens of detained miners who died in a crowded jail cell screamed for help as jailors ignored their suffering. And ahead of the Youth Olympics in Senegal, Kenya is ramping up support for its female athletes.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry></feed>
